From 24d542cc3485b4b79fac9ea6fd02c22c8ffcdf27 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josep Torra <n770galaxy@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 12:42:58 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 12/13] ##arch: Emulate the USSE forms of the second probe
 round

A second round of client fills on an SGX545 pinned more of what the
instruction text left open, and the ESIL follows the answers:

- write masks: component k writes d + k from every register source + k,
  a repeat of four with gaps (mov, the bitwise group and shifts,
  frcp/frsq/fsqrt, movc, the packs); mask 0 writes nothing
- .incsXYZ: X, Y and Z let source 0, 1 and 2 advance, the destination
  always advances, every source without .incs; fmad, fminmax and fmaxmin
  repeat in ascending order
- fdp.repeatN d, a, b writes the N-term dot product to d + N - 1 only,
  each product and then each sum rounded to binary32; fddp writes
  s0 . s1 there and s0 . s2 to i0/i1; fdpc and fddpc, whose clip-plane
  result is not located, get none
- fminmax d, a, b, c = min(max(a, b), c), fmaxmin = max(min(a, c), b),
  with IEEE minNum/maxNum (a NaN loses, -0 below +0), computed on the
  bit patterns
- movc.<type>.<test>: a select per 32/16/8-bit lane, three 10-bit lanes
  for .i10 (bits 30-31 cleared), or the float with denormals as zero
- movmsk.<mask|u8|flt|flt16>: s1 into d when bit 0 or bit 7 of byte c,
  or the float or half c, is at least 0.5 (.smsk is not modelled)
- pck<u8|s8|o8|u16|s16|c10>f32 and the unpacks to f32 and between 8- and
  16-bit integers: lanes, byte masks, saturation, scales and rounding as
  measured; f16 and c10 sources and f16 results are not modelled
- i3, which reads as i0 and drops writes, is no longer a register to
  the ESIL

8 new test/db/esil/usse tests. The microkernel uses none of these forms:
84.2% of its words still have ESIL; 425 of 153466 decodable random words
do (was 275).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
